  "description": "WebGPU rendering straight into SkiaSharp surfaces. Give it an SKSurface, an SKCanvas, a GRContext or nothing at all and it picks the fastest way to get WebGPU pixels onto it - zero copy when the surface lives on the same GPU device (Vulkan, Direct3D 12 or Metal), one GPU-side draw when it lives on the same device but its own texture cannot be shared, a CPU readback otherwise - and reports which one it took and why. Can create the GPU device and a SkiaSharp GRContext on it, or adopt the Vulkan or Metal device behind an application's own GRContext. Explicit, documented frame protocol for handing the texture between WebGPU and Skia; headless rendering to SKImage, SKBitmap or bytes. Built on CodeBrix.WebGpu.Native.",
